Anime Ultrascale
A Tool for Extreme Anime Upscaling.

-----------------------------------------------------

This README is dedicated to installation. For
usage information, run the program with '--help'.
For version information, refer to 'pyproject.toml'.

The program resides in the Python file
'anime-ultrascale.py', which can be used in any
system as long as a Python environment satisfying
"pyproject.toml" is installed.

An Ubuntu in-place installer is provided. To
install the program in Ubuntu, please follow the
following istructions:

1) Install Python, version 3.10 or later.

2) Install the python package 'venv', e.g. 'pip
   install venv'.

2) install the pyvips runtime, e.g. 'sudo apt
   install -y libvips42'.

3) Open a bash terminal at the current location
   and run:

chmod +x install
source ./install

Only this folder and '~/.bashrc' will be altered.
The program will be available as 'anime-ultrascale'
in both the installation terminal and all new bash
terminals of the current user.

